# L §7.6 item 1 (tally 2.1.7 B1, issue #150; T's SR-2): "A day computed outside them is refused: by ... a range's
# next key". near .. end31 step 1 day holds 9999-12-30 and 9999-12-31, and its next key would be past 9999-12-31:
# RUN-LIMIT `a day passes 9999-12-31` (r_two). near2 .. end30 ends a day before, so its next key is 9999-12-31 and it
# is answered (r_twin). 2.1.7's first refcore stopped at the last day there is and answered r_two 2; a range of
# 1 000 001 keys ending on 9999-12-31 was answered the same way (T's g14/day_range_end r_past).
=== sr2.tally
model sr2
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source plan "invented"

input n1: int

input end31: date

input end30: date

input near: date

input near2: date

ask r_two: sum(n1 for d in near .. end31 step 1 day)

ask r_twin: sum(n1 for d in near2 .. end30 step 1 day)

version v
  cite plan
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  n1 = 1 "one"
  end31 = 9999-12-31 "the calendar's last day"
  end30 = 9999-12-30 "the day before it"
  near = 9999-12-30 "a day before the last"
  near2 = 9999-12-29 "two days before the last"
=== expect
r_twin: 2
  cut 2026-12-31
r_two: refused: RUN-LIMIT a day passes 9999-12-31
  cut 2026-12-31
